-- title:
--   Incomparable branch ideals at a crossing point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, together with a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$; assume the Laurent series $j(q)$, namely `jqModC ℚ`, lies in the $q$-expansion function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, the bundle of data and properties for the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ over $R_p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, let $\rho : R_p \to A$ be a ring map whose composite with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map, let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O : R_p \to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, and let `toκ` $: O \to \kappa_A$ satisfy `toκ` $\circ\, \rho_O = \mathrm{res}_A \circ \rho$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,0$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,1$, and let $x_n = \mathfrak X.\mathrm{crossingPt}\,n$ be its image in `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO` under the first projection followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,0$ and the base-change map `bcMap`. Assume both $\mathfrak X.\xi_\infty$ and $\mathfrak X.\xi_0$ specialise to $x_n$. Then the two associated branch ideals of the local ring at $x_n$ — the preimages of the maximal ideals of the stalks at $\xi_0$, respectively $\xi_\infty$, under the stalk-specialisation maps — are incomparable: neither is contained in the other.
--
--   This supplies the "two distinct branches" input to the local analysis of a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ over a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$, the inclusion of one branch ideal in the other being equivalent to a specialisation between the generic points of the two components. It is used in the proofs that the germ of $p$ at a crossing point is a non-zero-divisor with stalk of Krull dimension at least $2$, and that oriented étale crossing charts exist.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_not_branchIdeal_le_branchIdeal_crossingPt.lean

